WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.837
Compute.

2
00:00:00.837 --> 00:00:04.184
Once identity, policy and
network services have moved,

3
00:00:04.184 --> 00:00:08.051
domain-joined machines are the
largest remaining dependency.

4
00:00:08.051 --> 00:00:12.905
A machine leaves only when its identity,
its policy and its trust have each

5
00:00:12.905 --> 00:00:17.362
been replaced, so the domain join is
the last thing to go, not the first.

6
00:00:17.362 --> 00:00:20.697
User PCs end Entra joined
and managed in Intune,

7
00:00:20.697 --> 00:00:24.288
and every hardware refresh
should arrive that way.

8
00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:28.739
Hybrid join is a transition: there's
no supported way to convert a

9
00:00:28.739 --> 00:00:33.526
hybrid-joined PC without resetting
it, so time that reset to a refresh.

10
00:00:33.526 --> 00:00:37.075
A program that leaves devices
hybrid joined hasn't finished.

11
00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:38.725
Servers take a different road.

12
00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:43.082
Azure Arc projects them into Azure
for policy and posture while they stay

13
00:00:43.082 --> 00:00:47.725
where they are, and leaving the domain is
a separate decision for each workload.

14
00:00:47.725 --> 00:00:50.600
What holds servers in the
domain is applications.

15
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.505
Every Kerberos service principal
name is an application,

16
00:00:54.505 --> 00:00:59.793
and each gets one of three answers: migrate
to modern authentication, retire it,

17
00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:05.000
or, as a last resort, keep it on a small
documented island with an end-of-life date.

18
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.075
NTLM is resolved in the same pass.

19
00:01:08.075 --> 00:01:12.838
And an application's compute stays with
its data until its round trips are reduced,

20
00:01:12.838 --> 00:01:15.500
because distance multiplies
with every call.

21
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.812
Only an application's owner can make
that call and sign off its cutover.

22
00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:25.491
Keeping legacy authentication open is
a risk acceptance, so the authorizing

23
00:01:25.491 --> 00:01:31.490
official sets every island and NTLM end
date, and every name is resolved by Gate G4.
